  "description": "The LLDP neighbor on node\u202f7 is reported on interface **GigabitEthernet0/1** (ifNumber\u202f101) of **Switch01**, a Cisco Catalyst\u202f2960. The chassis identifier is **00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E**, classified as a MAC\u202fAddress. The port identifier is **1**, using the Interface\u202fName subtype, and the port description is \u201cUplink\u202fPort\u201d. Autonegotiation is both supported and enabled (YES), with the advertised capabilities \u201c10BaseT,100BaseTXFD\u201d and the currently negotiated mode \u201c10BaseT\u201d. Autonegotiation support is confirmed (YES). The link\u2011aggregation feature is capable (YES) but not enabled (NO); the aggregation group number is **5**. Management address **192.168.1.1** is present, typed as IPv4, and the interface MTU is **1500** bytes with a TTL of **120** seconds. The interface flag is **0** and its type is reported as UNKNOWN.\n\nSystem capabilities are listed as \u201cBridge,\u202fRouter\u201d, with \u201cBridge\u201d enabled, and the system description echoes \u201cCisco Catalyst\u202f2960\u201d. The LLDP protocol identifier is **LLDP** (protocol ID). Port protocol details show ID\u202f2, supported\u202f3, and enabled\u202f1. VLAN information indicates the default VLAN (\u201cdefault\u201d, VLAN\u202fID\u202f1) on the port, while the port itself is assigned to VLAN\u202fID\u202f10. All other reported values\u2014node ID\u202f7, port VLAN ID\u202f10, and the protocol ID\u2014are consistent with the observed configuration."
